  "scope_warning": "The formal main upper-bound proof is complete: eleven paper lemmas, the obstruction proposition, actual correcting-code existence, and the optimal redundancy bound are kernel-checked. For every t >= 2, all sufficiently large n admit a nonempty binary code correcting any combination of at most t insertions/deletions in total, with redundancy <= (2*t-1)*log_2(n) + (6*b_t+6)*log_2(log_2(n)), where b_t=4*a_t+2 and a_t=100*t*(32*t+17). The minimum redundancy is defined using the proved attained maximum size of all actual correcting codes. All witness counts, random-hash probabilities, discard estimates, selection, and large-n thresholds are derived. The whole-manuscript flag stays false because historical literature claims and external results in the surrounding prose are not formalized; no step of this main-proof chain remains assumed. Mathematical correspondence between paper prose and formal definitions remains a human-review responsibility.",
